  "knowledgePattern": "Convert modulus constraints to independent intervals and attain the product bound",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Turn each modulus into an interval",
      "body": "<p>Rearrange each condition into the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></math>. This says <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow></math> is at most <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow></math> units from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "A modulus bound gives the two ends of an allowed interval.",
      "pitfall": "In the condition on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></math>, divide every term by the same positive factor.",
      "pause": "Find the full allowed interval for each variable.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l04",
          "reminder": "A modulus bound gives the two ends of an allowed interval."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Choose the smallest absolute factors",
      "body": "<p>Mark the allowed intervals on a number line. For each variable, choose the allowed value closest to zero.</p>",
      "recap": "The modulus of a product is the product of the moduli.",
      "pitfall": "Check that your three chosen values can satisfy the conditions at the same time.",
      "pause": "Multiply their absolute values and check the proposed minimum is possible.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b3-l01",
          "reminder": "Convert modulus bounds to intervals and check that proposed product extremes can occur together."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p><strong>1.</strong> The inequalities give <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></math>. Thus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>2.</strong> All three factors are positive. Therefore <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>3.</strong> The constraints are independent, so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> satisfies all three and attains the bound. The least value is 8, answer E.</p>"
}
